 blockers but do not deepen ARC. The freshest, validated, operator-hands-on
 lever (docs/research-notes/arc-config-layerb-scaffolded-2026-06-18.md): a
 local offline gemma-4-12B that CANNOT read a raw 64x64 scene CAN induce a
 GROUNDED relational win-RULE when handed object-centric digests (ka59 reached
 Tier-2 count_4==32, fires-on-win, 0 false-positives), and the verifier
 GROUNDS/REJECTS the proposed predicate (propose-then-ground). The operator's
 first-contact audit names the 9 toggle/CONFIG games (bp35, dc22, g50t, ka59,
 lf52, s5i5, tn36, sc25, tr87) as 'the clear #1 next investment and the
 genuinely hard one' -- target-PATTERN (win-rule) induction over a 40-210-cell
 editable space random exploration cannot stumble. THE STEP: REUSE the
 validated scaffolded inducer
 (scripts/experiments/arc3_config_layerb_scaffolded.py) -- object-centric
 digest (editable bbox + value counts; reference connected-component features,
 NEVER a raw grid) -> local gemma-12B-Q4 on the iGPU proposes is_win(grid) ->
 the verifier GROUNDS it on the banked win + non-wins -> wire the grounded
 predicate as the OfflineSolver verifier (arc_solver_kit) to drive a
 best-first search to the NEXT level. Targets (per-game checkpoint + wall-time
 cap; breadth beats all-or-nothing): ka59 L2 (rule known -> drive the solve) +
 FIRST-CONTACT win-rule grounding on >=2 UNSOLVED config games
 (bp35/dc22/g50t/lf52/s5i5). HARD gate per target: a NEW level
 offline_reproduced=true beyond the prior reproduced best
 (arc_solver_kit.reproduce) OR a Tier-2 GROUNDED win-rule for a NEW config
 game (honest partial -- the rule grounds; the search-to-win is the logged
 residual). verifier_is_oracle=true (the SOLVE is execution-grounded -- ARC
 progress, NOT an oracle-distinct moat headline; the contribution is that the
 verifier GROUNDS the LLM-proposed rule). The local gemma-12B runs on the iGPU
 ONLY (never the 3090s), offline-legal, zero quota. NO TRM training; NO
 leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH target.

